Candidate algorithm: for each nonempty block B, compute rejection mask R(B)
of negatives whose B-projection is absent from all positive B-projections.
A valid partition is an exact cover of symbols whose rejection-mask union
covers all negatives, with block count in K. Canonical recursion uses the
least remaining symbol in the next block. Memoized DP may count/retrieve answers
and constrained pair alternatives without materializing all Bell partitions.
This is exponential, not a polynomial-time or general speed claim.
An independent RGS enumerator must compare complete sets on small cases.
Pairs require existence proofs/countermodels for both possible relations;
positive-only default ALL partitions remain feasible.

